## Feature Details

### FG1: Pattern Editor

#### 1.1 Grid Editor (enhanced) — CRITICAL
- Canvas with pannable, zoomable grid
- Cell size adjustable (4px to 48px)
- Alternating cell shading (counting aid) — configurable colors
- Row/column labels — 1-based numbering, configurable start, configurable font size
- Large grid support (up to 500×500) via virtualized rendering

##### FG1.1A: Multi-weight Grid Lines (MOST URGENT FIX)
**This is the single biggest UX improvement for the grid editor.**

The current app has all grid lines at the same thin weight. Competitors use **visual hierarchy** in the grid lines to make counting practical:

- **Light grid lines** — every cell border (very thin, subtle gray, ~0.5-1px)
- **Medium grid lines** — every 5 stitches (bold, darker, ~2px) — creates counting blocks
- **Heavy grid lines** — every 10 stitches (bold + darkest, ~2-3px) — creates major divisions
- **Number labels** change at heavy line intervals (bold, larger font, darker color)
- **Number labels** also change at medium line intervals (slightly bolder)

**Implementation details:**
```typescript
interface GridLineConfig {
  lightLineColor: string;    // every cell — e.g., '#e5e7eb'
  lightLineWidth: number;    // e.g., 0.5
  mediumInterval: number;    // every N stitches — e.g., 5
  mediumLineColor: string;   // e.g., '#9ca3af'
  mediumLineWidth: number;   // e.g., 2
  heavyInterval: number;     // every N stitches — e.g., 10  
  heavyLineColor: string;    // e.g., '#4b5563'
  heavyLineWidth: number;    // e.g., 3
}
```

**Rendering approach:**
- Three layered overlays (not single-pass): light on bottom, medium on middle, heavy on top
- Or: single-pass with conditional lineWidth per border
- Use CSS box-shadow inset for grid lines (avoids double-line issue at intersections)
- Number labels rendered in a separate layer outside the grid
- Labels only visible when zoom > threshold (hide at high zoom to save space)
- Label interval: every 1 stitch, but only shown at every 5 when zoom is low

**Competitor reference — Stitch Fiddle:**
- Every 5 cells: darker vertical and horizontal lines
- Every 10 cells: even darker lines
- Row/column numbers change to bold/darker at heavy line boundaries
- Numbers on both left AND top edges
- Label font is large and readable even from a distance

**Competitor reference — Stitches Plus:**
- Configurable grid line weight at any interval
- Grid lines can be different colors for different intervals
- Numbers can be on edges only, or on both edges
- "Block mode" — numbers only at every N cells instead of every 1

##### FG1.1B: Label Configuration
- Label position: left edge only, right edge only, both, or none
- Label start number: 1-based or 0-based (some stitchers prefer 0-based)
- Label interval: every 1, 5, or 10 (block mode)
- Label font size: configurable (small/medium/large)
- Label font color: configurable
- Show labels even when grid lines are hidden (standalone mode)
- Label color can match the medium/heavy line color for visual coherence

#### 1.2 Drawing Tools
- **Pencil** — single stitch fill
- **Eraser** — clear stitch
- **Fill (Flood)** — flood-fill connected region of same color (BFS)
- **Line** — Bresenham line tool for backstitch outlines
- **Rectangle** — draw filled or outline rectangles
- **Circle** — draw filled or outline circles
- **Dropper/Color Picker** — sample color from canvas
- **Select & Move** — select region, move to another location
- **Copy/Paste** — copy selection to clipboard (within or across panels)
- **Mirror/Flip** — mirror selection horizontally or vertically
- **Brush** — multi-stitch brush (adjustable width)
- **Erase Line** — erase along a line path

#### 1.3 Backstitch Layer (NEW)
- Separate backstitch layer overlaying the main stitch grid
- Draw continuous lines between grid points
- Line width configurable (1px, 2px, 3px stitch widths)
- Line color independent of thread colors
- Can be toggled visible/hidden in editing mode
- Rendered in final output as solid lines between stitch centers
- Symbol mode: backstitch rendered as solid lines, not symbols
- Backstitch lines stored as `[{x1,y1,x2,y2,color}]` per panel

#### 1.4 Symbol System (enhanced)
- Auto-assign symbols (A-Z, a-z, 0-9, then Greek, special chars)
- **Manual symbol editing** — click a color swatch in palette to reassign its symbol
- **Symbol style selector** — circle, square, triangle, diamond, star, heart, cross, dot, custom
- **Symbol size** — configurable relative to cell size
- **Symbol color** — override per-color symbol fill/outlined colors
- **Symbol legend** — auto-generated, sorted by usage count
- **Custom symbols** — allow Unicode characters and simple SVG shapes
- **No-symbol mode** — solid color blocks only

##### FG1.1C: Label Visibility Rules
- When zoom < 50%: show numbers only at every 10 (to avoid crowding)
- When zoom 50-100%: show numbers at every 5
- When zoom > 100%: show numbers at every 1
- Labels always visible for the current row/column being edited (highlighted)
- When panning/zooming, labels auto-adjust based on current zoom level
- **Color blocks** — solid color cells
- **Symbol only** — symbols on white background
- **Color with symbols** — colored cells with symbol overlay
- **Counting view** — alternating cell colors + numbered rows/cols
- **3D preview** — WebGL preview of finished project (existing)
- **Zoom ranges**: 25% to 800%
- **Pan**: mouse drag or arrow keys

#### 1.6 Undo/Redo
- Configurable history depth (default 50)
- Per-panel history
- Keyboard shortcuts: Ctrl+Z, Ctrl+Shift+Z

#### 1.7 Multiple Panels
- Support for multi-panel designs (quilts, banners, 3D objects)
- Rename/delete/add panels
- Link panels (shared color palette)
- Panel tabs for switching
- Grid dimensions per panel (flexible layout)

---

### FG2: Image-to-Chart

#### 2.1 Image Upload
- JPG, PNG, GIF, WebP, BMP
- Drag-and-drop + file picker
- URL paste (from clipboard)
- Image preview with aspect ratio lock

#### 2.2 Stitch Width Estimation
- Canvas size in stitches (width × height)
- Stitch size in mm (configurable per fabric)
- Fabric type: Aida 11/14/16/18ct, Evenweave 14/16/18ct, Linen
- Aspect ratio lock toggle
- Auto-calculate stitch size from image dimensions

#### 2.3 Color Quantization (ENHANCED)
- **K-Means clustering** (k-means++) for color reduction
- **Mahalanobis distance** to DMC palette (better than Euclidean)
- **Configurable max colors** (2 to 128)
- **Preserve dominant colors** — option to keep specific colors (e.g., skin tones, backgrounds)
- **Color grouping** — group similar colors into one DMC shade

#### 2.4 Dithering (NEW)
- **Floyd-Steinberg dithering** — for photorealistic results
- **Sierra 3-2-1 dithering** — lighter, smoother results
- **Stucki dithering** — alternative for smooth gradients
- **No dithering** — clean color blocks
- Toggle dithering on/off, adjustable threshold

#### 2.5 Post-Conversion Cleanup Tools
- **Reduce colors** — merge similar colors post-conversion
- **Increase colors** — split dominant colors
- **Smoothing** — remove single-stitch noise (median filter)
- **Isolate noise** — find and select single isolated stitches
- **Batch recolor** — select all stitches of color X, change to color Y
- **Crop tool** — trim blank borders from converted image
- **Resize tool** — resize grid after conversion (nearest-neighbor)

#### 2.6 Color Swapping
- Click palette color, click target color → swap all occurrences
- Range swap — select color range and replace
-eyedropper on canvas → pick color to swap

---

### FG3: Export & Print

#### 3.1 PDF Pattern Export (enhanced)
- Page size: A4, A5, Letter, Legal, Custom
- Orientation: Portrait, Landscape
- **Symbol view** — grid with symbols
- **Color block view** — solid colors
- **Half-cross view** — show X with diagonal lines
- **Thread legend** — DMC numbers, color swatches, thread count, estimated skeins
- **Multiple pages** — for large patterns, split across pages with continuity markers
- **Bold/stitch count labels** — row/column numbers at intervals (every 5/10)
- **Title/author** on first page
- **Page numbering** with "page X of Y"
- **Scale reference** — printed stitch size reference

#### 3.2 Shopping List Export (enhanced)
- Per-color thread usage (stitches, cm, estimated skeins)
- Multiple floss brands shown
- Checkbox list (printable)
- Sort by: color number, usage (descending), alphabetical
- **Thread length calculator** — accounts for strand count (1, 2, or 3 strands)

#### 3.3 Written Instructions (NEW)
- Row-by-row text description of the pattern
- Format: "Row 1: 3×BL, 5×RD, 2×BL, 8×WH, ..."
- Abbreviated: use first letters of color names
- Group consecutive same-color stitches
- **Abbreviation dictionary** — customizable
- **Export formats**: PDF, TXT, Markdown
- **Reading direction**: left-to-right, right-to-left, top-to-bottom
- **Notation options**: numeric codes, color names, symbols

#### 3.4 QR Code (NEW)
- Generate QR code linking to:
  - PDF download
  - Online pattern view
  - Progress tracker (if online)
- Embed in PDF as small corner element
- Scan with phone to view pattern while stitching

---

### FG4: Progress & Tracking

#### 4.1 Progress Tracking
- **Mark stitches as completed** — long-press or shift-click
- Color-coded completed stitches (dimmed/faded or checkmark overlay)
- **Progress bar** per panel and overall
- **Percentage complete** calculation
- **Save progress** — auto-save completed state separately from design

#### 4.2 Stitch Counter
- Manual stitch counter (tap to increment)
- Reset per row, per panel
- Visual indicator of current row/column while stitching

#### 4.3 Pattern Notes
- Add notes to specific rows or areas
- Pin comments to grid coordinates
- Notes appear as small markers on the grid

---

### FG5: Floss Brands & Library

#### 5.1 Multi-Brand Support
- **DMC** — 500+ colors (full)
- **Anchor** — 400+ colors
- **Madeira Mouline** — 379 colors
- **DMC Cross Stitch** — DMC's own cross-stitch line
- **DMC Metallic** — metallic threads
- **DMC Pearl Cotton** — perlé cotton
- **Generic/custom** — add any color with hex code

#### 5.2 Color Matching
- Cross-reference colors across brands
- "Closest match" when a color isn't in the selected brand
- Show alternative brands that carry the same shade

#### 5.3 Pattern Library
- **Browse** — search/filter community patterns
- **Upload** — share your patterns
- **Download** — import others' patterns
- **Categories** — animals, flowers, quotes, landscapes, etc.
- **Rating & reviews**
- **Pattern details** — designer, thread count, dimensions, brand, colors used

---

### FG6: Additional Features

#### 6.1 Pattern Repeats
- Define a block of stitches to repeat
- Tile horizontally, vertically, or both
- Preview repeat pattern
- Export repeat as new pattern

#### 6.2 Mirroring
- Mirror entire design (left-right, top-bottom)
- Mirror selection (partial)
- Mirror and offset (for quilt blocks)

#### 6.3 Semi-Cross Stitches (NEW)
- Upper-left half, upper-right half, lower-left half, lower-right half
- Useful for diagonal details in faces, flowers
- Represented as quarter-symbols in symbol mode

#### 6.4 Watermarks (NEW)
- Add watermark text to PDF exports
- "For personal use only"
- Designer name visible on pattern

#### 6.5 Keyboard Shortcuts
- Full keyboard shortcut system
- Configurable shortcuts
- Common: 1-9 for tool selection, Ctrl+Z undo, Ctrl+S save, etc.

#### 6.6 Responsive Design
- Desktop: full editor with panels
- Tablet: simplified editor, touch-friendly
- Phone: progress tracking + view-only mode

---

## Data Model

```typescript
interface CrossStitchProject {
  // Metadata
  title: string;
  author: string;
  description?: string;
  tags?: string[];
  category?: string;
  flossBrand: FlossBrand;
  fabric: FabricType;
  stitchCount: { width: number; height: number };
  created: Date;
  modified: Date;
  
  // Panels
  panels: Panel[];
  
  // Floss library
  flossLibrary: FlossBrand[];
  colorSwaps: Map<string, string>; // oldColor -> newColor
  
  // Settings
  settings: {
    showGridLines: boolean;
    showAlternatingColors: boolean;
    showRowLabels: boolean;
    showColLabels: boolean;
    gridLineSpacing: number; // every N rows/cols
    alternatingColorEven: string;
    alternatingColorOdd: string;
    labelFontSize: number;
  };
  
  // Progress
  progress: {
    completedStitches: Set<string>; // "panelId:row:col"
    notes: Note[];
  };
}

interface Panel {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  shape: 'rectangle' | 'pentagon' | 'hexagon' | 'custom';
  design: Cell[][]; // 2D grid of Cell objects
  backstitch: BackstitchLine[];
  status: 'not-started' | 'in-progress' | 'finished';
}

interface Cell {
  colorIndex: number; // index into palette
  // For semi-cross: partial color info
  semiCross?: SemiCrossType; // 'upper-left' | 'upper-right' | 'lower-left' | 'lower-right'
}

type SemiCrossType = 'upper-left' | 'upper-right' | 'lower-left' | 'lower-right';

interface BackstitchLine {
  id: string;
  x1: number; y1: number;
  x2: number; y2: number;
  color: string; // hex
  lineWidth: number; // in stitch widths
}

interface FlossBrand {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  colors: FlossColor[];
  logo?: string;
}

interface FlossColor {
  number: string; // e.g., "824"
  name: string;   // e.g., "Pine Green"
  hex: string;     // e.g., "#3D5337"
  rgb: { r: number; g: number; b: number };
  crossRefs?: { [brand: string]: string }; // DMC 824 -> Anchor 1182
}

interface Note {
  id: string;
  x?: number; // row
  y?: number; // col
  text: string;
  created: Date;
}
```

---

## Technical Stack

- **Framework**: React 19 + TypeScript
- **Build**: Vite 8
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS 4
- **State**: Zustand (persist with localStorage + optional IndexedDB for large grids)
- **3D**: React Three Fiber + Three.js (existing)
- **PDF**: jsPDF + autoTable (existing)
- **QR Code**: qrcode.react
- **Color Quantization**: color-quantize (k-means) + custom DMC distance function
- **Dithering**: Custom Floyd-Steinberg implementation
- **Icons**: Lucide React (existing)
- **Virtualization**: react-window for large grids
